+# Activities
+
+## `GET /:account_slug/activities.json`
+
+Returns account activity as a flat array, newest activity first. Only events on boards the current user can access are returned.
+
+| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
+|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
+| `creator_ids[]` | array of strings | No | Only return events created by these users |
+| `board_ids[]` | array of strings | No | Only return events on these boards |
+
+Multiple IDs within a filter are combined with OR. When both filters are provided, events must match both. Filtering never grants access to otherwise inaccessible activity.
+
+__Example using curl:__
+
+```bash
+curl -G \
+  -H "Authorization: Bearer put-your-access-token-here" \
+  --data-urlencode "creator_ids[]=03f5v9zjw7pz8717a4no1h8a7" \
+  --data-urlencode "board_ids[]=03f5v9zhwc6bj7wwb5w0c07b4" \
+  http://app.fizzy.localhost:3006/686465299/activities.json
+```
+
+### Event types
+
+Activity includes the following actions:
+
+- `card_assigned`
+- `card_unassigned`
+- `card_published`
+- `card_closed`
+- `card_reopened`
+- `card_board_changed`
+- `card_postponed`
+- `card_auto_postponed`
+- `card_title_changed`
+- `card_triaged`
+- `card_sent_back_to_triage`
+- `comment_created`
+
+These mirror the HTML activity timeline, except that deprecated `card_collection_changed` events are omitted and `card_title_changed` events are included.
+
+### Response
+
+Returns `200 OK` with an array of events, or an empty array when no events match. Each event contains:
+
+| Field | Description |
+|-------|-------------|
+| `id` | The event's ID |
+| `action` | One of the event types listed above |
+| `created_at` | When the event occurred, as an ISO 8601 timestamp in UTC |
+| `description` | The event's plain-text description |
+| `particulars` | Event-specific details, described below |
+| `url` | A URL opening the card; for comments, it opens the parent card and jumps to the comment |
+| `eventable_type` | `Card` or `Comment` |
+| `eventable` | The existing [card](cards.md) or [comment](comments.md) API representation |
+| `board` | The existing [board](boards.md) API representation |
+| `creator` | The existing [user](users.md) API representation for the event's creator |
+
+### Particulars
+
+The `particulars` object contains only the details relevant to the event's action:
+
+| Action | Particulars |
+|--------|-------------|
+| `card_assigned`, `card_unassigned` | `{"assignee_ids": ["user_id"]}` |
+| `card_board_changed` | `{"old_board": "Old board name", "new_board": "New board name"}` |
+| `card_title_changed` | `{"old_title": "Old title", "new_title": "New title"}` |
+| `card_triaged` | `{"column": "Column name"}` |
+| All other actions | `{}` |
+
+Missing board names, titles, and column names are returned as empty strings, not `null`.
+
+### Pagination
+
+This endpoint follows the [standard API pagination conventions](../README.md#pagination), with page sizes that can vary. Follow the `Link` response header's `rel="next"` URL to retrieve subsequent pages. The next-page URL preserves the filters. The `X-Total-Count` header contains the total number of matching, accessible events.
diff --git a/test/controllers/activities_controller_test.rb b/test/controllers/activities_controller_test.rb
